<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech lower house rejects excise tax hikes-agency.</title>
<headline>Czech lower house rejects excise tax hikes-agency.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lower house of Czech parliament on Tuesday rejected an amended government proposal to raise excise taxes on cigarettes, alcohol and fuel, the CTK news agency reported.</p>
<p>It said the two right-wing parties in the ruling coalition voted against the plan after their centrist coalition partners, the Christian Democrats, joined the opposition to add an amendment to the plan which would have given tax breaks on diesel fuel for farmers.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
